SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Censure motion filed, targets Prayut, 10 others","publisher":"Bangkok Post / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-06-15","url":"https://www.bangkokpost.com/thailand/politics/2326903/censure-motion-filed-targets-prayut-10-others","claim":"Opposition parties filed a no-confidence motion accusing Prayut and other cabinet ministers of graft, intentional constitutional and ethics violations, and condoning corrupt practices; the government spokesman replied that the government had run the country honestly without corruption.","locator":"article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters-reported parliamentary coverage with detailed, contemporaneous allegations and a quoted government response.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Prayut as prime minister and the government he led; the underlying claims are opposition allegations rather than independent findings.","contrary_evidence":["The article reports allegations, not a finding of corruption or dishonesty."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Prayut counters censure attack as lacking in correct information","publisher":"Nation Thailand","publication_date":"2022-07-19","url":"https://www.nationthailand.com/in-focus/40017920","claim":"Prayut told parliament that the opposition debate contained incorrect information and said the opposition had distorted facts to create public confusion; the story frames this as his direct reply to the censure motion.","locator":"article body and quoted remarks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Thai reporting with direct attributed remarks from Prayut in Parliament.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within the target year and during the censure debate.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Prayut's public statements.","contrary_evidence":["This is a self-defense claim, not external verification that his critics were wrong."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Prayut will answer opposition questions during censure showdown: govt spokesman","publisher":"Nation Thailand","publication_date":"2022-04-27","url":"https://www.nationthailand.com/in-focus/40014969","claim":"The government spokesman said Prayut was confident he had done nothing wrong and would answer every issue raised by the opposition, while accusing opponents of distorting information.","locator":"article body and quoted spokesman remarks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Attributed contemporaneous reporting on the prime minister's public posture before the censure debate.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Prayut through his spokesman and public stance.","contrary_evidence":["The report records his denial, not a finding that no wrongdoing occurred."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Censure motion filed, targets Prayut, 10 others","publisher":"Bangkok Post","publication_date":"2022-06-15","url":"https://www.bangkokpost.com/thailand/politics/2326903/censure-motion-filed-targets-prayut-10-others","claim":"The opposition's motion said the government had failed in administration, intentionally violated the constitution and ethical standards, condoned corrupt practices, and failed to implement its policies; the piece also notes Prayut's coalition was expected to survive the vote.","locator":"article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed contemporaneous report of the opposition's public charges and the government's likely political survival.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"These are allegations aimed at Prayut and his cabinet, not independent integrity findings.","contrary_evidence":["The source does not establish the truth of the allegations."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Thai PM Survives 4th No-Confidence Vote in Parliament","publisher":"Reuters via VOA","publication_date":"2022-07-23","url":"https://www.voanews.com/a/thai-pm-survives-4th-no-confidence-vote-in-parliament-/6670722.html","claim":"Reuters reported that Prayut survived a no-confidence vote after four days of grilling over accusations of corruption and economic mismanagement; the report also notes that he gave no indication of when an election would be called.","locator":"article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire story with parliamentary vote totals and contemporaneous allegations.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly about Prayut and his government, but the corruption accusations remain allegations.","contrary_evidence":["Surviving a no-confidence vote does not itself prove honesty or dishonesty."],"lenses":["7B.7","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"'No reshuffle,' says defiant PM","publisher":"Bangkok Post","publication_date":"2022-07-23","url":"https://www.bangkokpost.com/thailand/politics/2352066/no-reshuffle-says-defiant-pm","claim":"Prayut denied a cabinet reshuffle was imminent, said he had the final say, and the report says he met a coalition MP group seeking support for the cabinet and discussed maintaining coalition unity.","locator":"article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous reporting with direct attributed remarks and coalition-pressure details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year political maneuvering during the censure period.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Prayut as prime minister managing cabinet and coalition ties.","contrary_evidence":["This shows coalition management, but not necessarily personal dishonesty or self-dealing by itself."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.8","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Suspended Thai PM Prayuth says to continue as defence minister","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-08-25","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/suspended-thai-pm-prayuth-says-to-continue-as-defence-minister-2880424","claim":"After the Constitutional Court suspended him as prime minister pending term-limit review, Prayut said on social media he would continue as defence minister and made his first direct public address after the order.","locator":"article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire report on an immediate, attributable response to a court order.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Prayut's own decision after the court suspension.","contrary_evidence":["Continuing as defence minister is not itself proof of concealment or honesty; it is a legal and political move."],"lenses":["7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Thai court rules prime minister can stay in office","publisher":"The Japan Times / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-09-30","url":"https://www.japantimes.co.jp/news/2022/09/30/asia-pacific/politics-diplomacy-asia-pacific/prayut-term-limit-ruling/","claim":"Thailand's Constitutional Court ruled that Prayut had not exceeded the eight-year limit, allowing him to return from suspension and continue in office.","locator":"article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire story reproducing the court ruling with clear legal consequence.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"This is a legal outcome about Prayut's tenure, not a proof of personal honesty; it matters here because it bears on his stated commitment to formal limits.","contrary_evidence":["The court ruling does not resolve whether his tenure strategy was ethically candid or opportunistic."],"lenses":["7B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Prayut will join new party: source","publisher":"Bangkok Post","publication_date":"2022-11-11","url":"https://www.bangkokpost.com/thailand/politics/2434944/prayut-will-join-new-party-source","claim":"A party source said Prayut was being courted to join the newly established Ruam Thai Sang Chart Party after the APEC summit, and that some MPs were expected to follow him there.","locator":"article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous reporting on party-switch plans, though based on a source rather than a direct public announcement.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late-2022 target-period political maneuvering.","ruler_attribution":"About Prayut's own political choice and surrounding support network.","contrary_evidence":["This is still source-based reporting before his final public confirmation."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.8","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Prayut's future still under wraps after report of crucial meeting","publisher":"Bangkok Post","publication_date":"2022-11-22","url":"https://www.bangkokpost.com/thailand/politics/2443647/","claim":"The report says Prayut's political future remained under wraps amid reports that he might join Ruam Thai Sang Chart, with insiders describing continuing coalition maneuvering over his post-election role.","locator":"article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous but source-heavy reporting on an unresolved political move.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Late-2022 target-period context.","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to Prayut's own political positioning, but the report is not itself a direct statement from him.","contrary_evidence":["It is better treated as transitional context than as a concrete act."],"lenses":["7B.8","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"At last, Prayut will run for PM under Ruam Thai Sang Chart banners","publisher":"Thai Newsroom","publication_date":"2022-12-23","url":"https://thainewsroom.com/2022/12/23/at-last-prayut-will-run-for-pm-under-ruam-thai-sang-chart-banners/","claim":"Prayut confirmed he would register with Ruam Thai Sang Chart and run for head of government under that party's banner, after previously remaining non-committal about his political future.","locator":"article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Direct reporting on a late-2022 public confirmation, though from a smaller local outlet.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Prayut's own political choice.","contrary_evidence":["The source is secondary and smaller than Reuters, so it is best used as supportive context rather than a standalone anchor."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.8","7B.9","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Prayut promises to free Thailand of corruption, introduce transparency","publisher":"Nation Thailand","publication_date":"2022-12-09","url":"https://www.nationthailand.com/thailand/policies/40022926","claim":"At an anti-corruption event, Prayut said Thailand was mired in corruption, pledged to fight graft, and said he was paying close attention to punishing wrongdoers and ensuring transparent operations.","locator":"article body and quoted remarks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct reporting of a public anti-corruption speech with clear quotes.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Prayut's own public claims, though they are self-reports rather than independent findings.","contrary_evidence":["The speech is a promise and self-description, not evidence that corruption was actually reduced."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022/95 'Dissecting Thailand's 2022 Military and Police Reshuffles: Palace Proactivity?'","publisher":"ISEAS - Yusof Ishak Institute","publication_date":"2022-12-06","url":"https://www.iseas.edu.sg/articles-commentaries/iseas-perspective/2022-95-dissecting-thailands-2022-military-and-police-reshuffles-palace-proactivity-by-paul-chambers","claim":"The study says Prayut and Prawit appointed their favourites to senior army and police posts, and that 2022 reshuffles were heavily influenced by political and personal ties and factional bargaining.","locator":"executive summary and reshuffle analysis sections","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Analytical scholarly source with concrete tables and a detailed 2022 appointment map.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly focused on 2022 appointments and reshuffles.","ruler_attribution":"Strongly attributable to Prayut and his close governing network because the paper explicitly names them as appointment influencers.","contrary_evidence":["The paper also stresses that palace influence was substantial, so not every appointment can be attributed solely to Prayut."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Thai court won't rule on PM's oath omitting duty to constitution","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2019-09-11","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2019/09/11/thai-court-wont-rule-on-pms-oath-omitting-duty-to-constitution","claim":"Reuters reported that Prayuth Chan-ocha and 35 cabinet ministers swore loyalty to the king but omitted the oath line promising to uphold and comply with the constitution.","locator":"article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report on a formal, documented oath omission with direct public consequences.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 background that remained relevant in 2022 because it bears on formal-commitment and ethical-example patterns.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Prayut and his cabinet at the swearing-in ceremony.","contrary_evidence":["This is an older event, so it is background evidence rather than target-year conduct."],"lenses":["7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"NACC told to disclose govt leaders' assets","publisher":"Bangkok Post","publication_date":"2021-08-08","url":"https://www.bangkokpost.com/thailand/general/2161679/nacc-told-to-disclose-govt-leaders-assets","claim":"The OIC said the NACC should disclose assets previously declared by Prayut and Wissanu, after critics said the pair exploited a legal loophole that let them avoid renewed public scrutiny; the piece notes Prayut's 2014 public asset declaration of 128 million baht and his later voluntary but undisclosed declarations.","locator":"article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Specific, dated reporting on an official transparency dispute involving Prayut's own asset declarations and the public-record question.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 transparency context that still governed the 2022 integrity environment.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Prayut's asset-disclosure situation, though the reporting concerns legal loopholes rather than proven illicit enrichment.","contrary_evidence":["The article does not prove personal profiteering; it shows opacity and a scrutiny gap."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Thai king swears in coup leader's cabinet","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2019-07-16","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2019/07/16/thai-king-swears-in-coup-leaders-cabinet","claim":"Reuters said critics viewed Prayut's 2019 cabinet lineup as giving important government positions to loyalists, even as the government said it was returning Thailand to normal democracy after the election.","locator":"article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on cabinet formation and criticism of loyalist appointments.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Older background relevant to the 2022 integrity pattern.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Prayut's cabinet formation choices, though the criticism is external assessment rather than a formal finding.","contrary_evidence":["It is background evidence and does not isolate 2022 conduct."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I considered roughly thirty documents across Reuters mirrors, Bangkok Post, Nation Thailand, Thai Newsroom, ISEAS, NACC/OIC material, and older Reuters reports on oath and cabinet formation. I kept sources that had a direct personal nexus to Prayut or his close governing network, or that established a concrete 2022 commitment/party-switch/term-limit pattern. I rejected or downgraded several classes of material: broad corruption indices and country-level governance metrics without personal attribution; human-rights or media-freedom reports that showed repression but not integrity nexus; pure economic or social-policy coverage; and repeated coverage of the same censure or term-limit episode when it added no new factual claim. I also treated some opposition allegations as context only, not as findings.

**Remaining gaps**
1. I still do not have a clean 2022 independent finding that Prayut personally lied, profited, or concealed an asset or contract. The evidence is strongest on coalition maneuvering, appointments, and transparency concerns, not on a proven enrichment case.
2. Asset and beneficial-interest evidence remains thin for 2022. A direct NACC record, court finding, or investigative report on Prayut's own declarations would materially improve 7B.4 and 7B.6.
3. Appointment evidence is better, but it is still partly mediated by scholarly analysis and coalition reporting. A primary cabinet-order trail or official appointment rationale would sharpen attribution.
4. If you want a tighter dossier, more search would help on 2022 asset disclosure, procurement, and any official record tied to Prayut's own declarations or corrections.
